const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文发展预平均方法，在高频观测受微观结构噪声影响时估计波动率相关量。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The article develops pre-averaging methods for estimating volatility-related quantities when high-frequency observations are contaminated by microstructure noise. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它是连续时间统计框架，先对局部观测平均再估计；噪声假设、采样方案、窗口选择和渐近条件决定可用范围。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It is a continuous-time statistical framework that locally averages observations before estimation, with noise assumptions, sampling scheme, window choice, and asymptotics defining applicability. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要有序高频价格、时间戳、交易时段、异常和更正标记、采样间隔、预平均窗口以及明确的噪声和跳跃假设。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"A comparable implementation needs ordered high-frequency prices, timestamps, market-session rules, correction and outlier flags, sampling intervals, pre-averaging windows, and explicit noise and jump assumptions. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源在既定条件下提供噪声稳健估计思路，不会证明每个价格不规则现象都是噪声，或某个窗口对所有市场最优。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The paper supplies a noise-robust estimation approach under stated conditions; it does not prove that every observed price irregularity is noise or that a chosen window is universally optimal. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"声明观测时钟和交易时间；保留原始与更正记录；记录窗口和采样选择；检查依赖与跳跃；将有限样本敏感性与渐近主张分开。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"State the observation clock and market hours; preserve raw versus corrected records; document window and sampling choices; check dependence and jumps; and evaluate finite-sample sensitivity separately from asymptotic claims. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record。连续时间假设和高频输入不能被粗粒度K线悄然替代，估计量也不是交易规则或实时风险保证。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record. Continuous-time assumptions and high-frequency inputs cannot be silently replaced by coarse bars, and the estimator is not a trading rule or real-time risk guarantee. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2008.11.004",label:{zh:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Stochastic Processes and their Applications · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Microstructure Noise in the Continuous Case: The Pre-Averaging Approach”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。连续时间假设和高频输入不能被粗粒度K线悄然替代，估计量也不是交易规则或实时风险保证。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Microstructure Noise in the Continuous Case: The Pre-Averaging Approach”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
